## Instructions

{% if intent == "OFFER_LETTER_BODY" %}
Draft the **free-text body of a formal offer letter** (not an email).
- Open with a formal salutation ("Dear {{ candidate_name }},").
- Express delight at extending the offer and briefly recap why the candidate stood out (1–2 sentences).
- State the role, department, and company clearly.
- Reference that detailed terms (compensation, benefits, joining date) are enumerated in the rest of the letter — DO NOT restate compensation numbers in this section; the template will render those.
- Outline next steps: review, sign electronically, submit onboarding documents.
- Close with welcome language and an HR contact placeholder ("{{HR_CONTACT}}").
- Keep tone {{ feedback_tone or "warm" }} but professional. Length: 4–6 short paragraphs.
- Use neutral, third-person language where appropriate; avoid emoji.

The "subject" field should contain a short letter title (e.g. "Letter of Offer — {{ role }}").
The "body" field is the formatted body text only.
{% elif decision == "SELECTED" %}
Draft a **congratulatory offer email**:
- Warm, professional tone
- Congratulate on selection
- Include role/designation details
- Include CTC and joining date if provided
- Outline next steps (document submission, onboarding)
- Express enthusiasm about them joining the team
{% else %}
Draft a **respectful rejection email**:
- Thank them genuinely for their time and interest
- Inform them of the decision without sharing specific negative feedback
- Encourage them to apply for future openings
- Maintain a positive, professional tone
- Keep it concise but empathetic
{% endif %}

